# Normalize text line endings in the repo, but never touch binary fixtures.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF
# inside the sample PDFs. That shifts every byte offset past the first newline,
# the xref table stops pointing at the objects it names, and pdfplumber fails
# with "Unexpected EOF" -- taking 28 tests down with it on checkout alone.
# The bid fixtures are the input the whole pipeline is proven against, so they
# have to survive a clone byte-for-byte.

* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.db    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
